  "about": "Difficulty 5. Four on the floor, so the accents sit on the off-beat eighths and the keys hook (0.75, 1.5, 2.5) against the kick; eighth doubles on the claps, sixteenth doubles only where the drums play sixteenths (3.5 / 3.75 in the second verse, 3 / 3.25 in the last hook); a build of quarters into straight eighths; freezes on both break bars; free-tap bars every beat after each called pair. CAPTURED MOVES (owner 2026-10-17, lane/dance-options): the kick step, the headstand and the moonwalk are spelled as the captures' ids (the same families, beats and accents: the scored steps, the cap and a flawless NORMAL score are unchanged); the side freeze stays the baby freeze. THE MOONWALK A PLAYER SEES is the first hook's first arm wave (khAm, beat 84: 4+ beats before the next step, and a move the cap keeps scored, so it plays whole); the last verse's moonwalk (kvD) is one of the moves the cap turns into a STYLE tap, as it always was. The last hook ends in a FREESTYLE section (kfreeFS: the same free taps, marked) — and, since 2026-10-17, so does the first (the same marked phrase in place of its last free phrase: the same slots, so the steps, the STYLE taps, the cap and a flawless score are unchanged): the buttons pick the move, MATCH is not asked, and it pays STYLE only. Accents, doubles and free taps are STYLE taps; only the moves are scored steps.",
